1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,196
Half of Costco's operating profit

2
00:00:02,196 --> 00:00:04,143
comes from a membership fee,

3
00:00:04,143 --> 00:00:05,880
not from the shelves.

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,500
Lets replicate it in Lagos.

5
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,300
Oke, a Lagos founder,

6
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,180
copies the model with one warehouse.

7
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:16,735
He sells grains, meat, oil and vegetables

8
00:00:16,735 --> 00:00:18,280
close to cost.

9
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:21,941
Members pay forty thousand naira a year to shop.

10
00:00:21,941 --> 00:00:24,680
The fee is where the profit lives.

11
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,992
He signs five thousand members.

12
00:00:26,992 --> 00:00:30,280
That is two hundred million naira in fees.

13
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:34,081
Each member spends one point two million naira a year.

14
00:00:34,081 --> 00:00:36,320
His profit: another two hundred million.

15
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:38,748
Total: four hundred million naira.

16
00:00:38,748 --> 00:00:42,220
Half of it landed before the first sale.

17
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:45,390
Costco members renew around nine times in ten,

18
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:48,020
so the fee comes back every year.

19
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:51,167
Take Oke to two hundred thousand members

20
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:54,520
and the fee alone is eight billion naira.

21
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:58,920
Investors and lenders want that renewal math on paper.

22
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:01,667
Maintrust Solutions writes the financial projections

23
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:04,620
and pitch deck behind a membership business.

24
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:07,620
DM us.

